<%= page_title @category.name.capitalize %>
<% page_metadata description: t("meta.descriptions.tag", category: @category.name),
                 record: @category %>

<%# Deliberately not cached as a whole. The works are listed in `position`
    order, and `Work.reposition` moves positions with `update_all`, so a
    reordering moves no timestamp this fragment could key on. Each preview
    caches itself on its own work, which is where the rendering cost is —
    and caching per work rather than per list is also what keeps the owner's
    drafts, which `visible` shows her here, out of a fragment the next
    anonymous visitor would read. %>
<div class="works-list">
  <%= render partial: 'works/work_preview', collection: @works, as: :work %>
</div>
